This project is open hardware and open source.

  * The hardware design -- everything under hardware/, the gerbers, BOM and
    placement files under out/, and the drawings and renders under docs/ --
    is licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive
    (CERN-OHL-P-2.0).  The full text is in LICENSE-HARDWARE.txt.

  * The scripts that generate and check it (make.py, scripts/, sim/) and the
    documentation text are licensed under the MIT License below.

The circuit is the discrete op-amp of Learning the Art of Electronics
(Thomas C. Hayes with Paul Horowitz, Cambridge University Press, 2016),
Lab 5L: a textbook lab exercise, drawn here from the book's description so
that it can be built and probed.  The book itself is copyrighted by its
authors and is not part of this repository.

